::ENG3_U01_L07_Q09::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Passage: The old bridge was missing two boards, but Theo crossed slowly, carrying a plank on his shoulder. He did not reach the other side alone; he stopped halfway and repaired the path behind him. Which paraphrase is most accurate? {
~A. Theo crosses quickly and ignores the broken bridge.#This contradicts his slow crossing and repair. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. Theo refuses to cross because the bridge is dangerous.#This contradicts his action. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=C. Theo moves forward while repairing the path so others can follow safely.#Correct. This captures both the action and meaning. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~D. Theo removes boards from the bridge for himself.#This is not supported by the passage. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

